  "output": {
    "file": "mesh-data.js",
    "bytes": 9269354,
    "sha256": "7ad2fb100188a173c7c16d3aa918480bc529f5e1763dc03e2a607c77ce8fe8e9",
    "encoding": "Base64 little-endian Float32 positions/normals; Uint32 triangle indices. Group start/count are index-buffer units."
  },
  "changes": [
    "OBJ vertex/normal tuples are converted to indexed buffers without global resampling, decimation or normalization.",
    "Source body hierarchy, visual local poses, 12 inherited joint definitions and home qpos are preserved from MJCF.",
    "Complete rectangular torso and head lettering regions are projected onto shared quadratic side-shell surfaces, fitted from surrounding unlettered shell strips. This includes glyph bottoms, walls, islands and adjacent shell vertices in base_3/base_4; transition strips use smooth blending.",
    "All fully projected region normals are replaced by analytic fitted-surface normals. Front tiny lettering and walls are flattened to x=0.327064 m, with matching black material. Exactly degenerate triangles are removed.",
    "Within mesh-data.js, all other mesh positions and normals remain as published, aside from shared front-region coordinates in base_2.",
    "Original text-only base_3 geometry is merged into the repaired shell. A complete positive-Y side cover is clipped from the merged surface at x=[-0.100,0.101] m and z=[0.011,0.055] m, and assigned to base_3 so exploded views contain a continuous generic panel. Only boundary-crossing triangles are split; there is no global retessellation.",
    "Runtime geometry and material modifications are recorded separately in runtimeChanges; the frozen mesh-data.js bytes are unchanged by those operations."
  ],
  "geometryAssurance": "Whole-region local surface reconstruction removes manufacturer text relief. Runtime refinements retain the rig and contact geometry. The integrating agent reviewed assembled and fully exploded browser views. This derivative is not manufacturer CAD or evidence of physical validation.",
